# Expert and Novice Solutions of Genetic Pedigree Problems.

**Authors:** Hackling, Mark W., Lawrence, Jeanette A.

## Abstract
Compares experts', advanced students', and novice students' use of genetics knowledge to generate and test hypotheses while solving genetic pedigree problems. Reports that experts identified more critical cues, tested more hypotheses, were more rigorous in the falsification of alternative hypotheses, and were more flexible to their solving strategies. (YP)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ380958

